// expect: refuse E_FieldOffsetUnprovable
// A field read whose receiver's row NOTHING closes: it is main's own
// parameter, so no literal anywhere in the program proves the shape. The
// layout is genuinely unknowable and the compile must REFUSE it — never a
// guessed offset 0, and since 2026-09-28 never a trap either: the settle
// point says it before a byte, where it had trapped at run time (134). The
// gate's other half is the refusal's TEXT: it names
// the selector and the receiver's live row, so a floor census is an
// inventory and not a count.
//
// This fixture used to carry the list-pattern shape below, which floored for
// a different reason — the twin key dropped the row var, so a body compiled
// against the decl's own unlearned row:
//
//     fn peek(frames) = match frames { [f, ..._] => f.slot, [] => 0 }
//     fn main(q) = peek([{other: 1, slot: 5}])
//
// That shape PROVES now and answers 5 (tests/rows/mn-proven-row-through-list).
// Its 134 was the limitation canonized, not the contract: the receiver's row
// did close, at the call, and the emit could not see it. The contract is what
// survives here — a row nothing closes still refuses.
fn peek(f) = f.slot

fn main(q) = peek(q)
